# The LIVE operational database. Tracked for the project's first 200-odd
# commits, which worked only while one machine ever wrote to it. The moment
# the Founder started using the app on their own machine, their copy diverged
# and `git pull` began aborting with "local changes would be overwritten" —
# silently stranding them three releases behind while every restart looked
# fine. A file that changes every time the program runs is state, not source.
# It is created on first run (opsdb.py init) and seeded by
# ops/idea-desk/seed_founder_idea.py; the decisions that matter are mirrored
# in git as ops/DECISIONS.md.
ops/db/operations.sqlite3
ops/db/operations.sqlite3-journal
ops/db/operations.sqlite3-wal
ops/db/operations.sqlite3-shm

# Scratch/test databases and reports — real test runs should use
# OPSDB_PATH pointed outside the repo (e.g. /tmp), but this is defense
# in depth in case one ever lands here by mistake. See ops/db/README.md.
ops/db/test*.sqlite3
ops/db/*.test.sqlite3
ops/db/*.CURRENT_STATUS.md
ops/db/*.overview.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Founder credential file (Milestone 2B4) — never committed. Wildcard
# also covers founder_auth.py's atomic-write temp file, which shares the
# same dot-prefixed .founder_credential stem. See
# ops/reviews/cto-milestone2b4-architecture.md §3/§13 and
# ops/control-center/founder_auth.py.
ops/control-center/.founder_credential*

# Raw agent output kept when an evaluation could not be read (TASK-024).
# Contains the Founder's idea and the agents' words — local diagnosis only.
ops/idea-desk/diagnostics/
